{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/wrangler.json",
  "name": "manut-api",
  // Tenant routes require a revocable device session. The operator bearer
  // secret (`wrangler secret put CLOUD_API_KEY`) works only on exact admin
  // methods behind a platform Access context matching ADMIN_ACCESS_AUD.
  // No admin audience is configured here: the owner must configure each
  // protected environment before use. Missing Access configuration denies.
  // Health stays public; auth exchange/refresh require ingress admission.
  // Inbound Linear webhooks verify against LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET, also a
  // Wrangler secret (`wrangler secret put LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET`), and stay
  // unreachable until the operator turns officeInbound on (OFFICE_INBOUND is
  // deliberately unset here). OFFICE_SHARING is unset for the same reason:
  // every OFC-21 sharing route refuses until officeSharing is turned on.
  // SHOP_FEED is unset too: GET /v1/feed, a shop's live feed, answers 403
  // feature_disabled until the operator turns shopFeed on (docs/turning-on.md).
  // RELAY_ENABLED is deliberately unset in every environment: until the owner
  // turns the relay on at gate G3, every /relay/ route answers 503
  // relay_disabled (docs/relay-protocol-v1.md, the kill switch).
  // Manut AI pilot (docs/pilot-api.md): three settings, none of them in this
  // file. APPROVAL_LINK_SECRET signs the owner's approval links and is a
  // Wrangler secret (`wrangler secret put APPROVAL_LINK_SECRET`, at least 32
  // random characters); without it no link is minted and every link is
  // invalid. WEB_ORIGIN (the approval page's origin, e.g. https://<web host>)
  // and PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN (this Worker's public origin, used in each LINE
  // webhook URL) are plain Worker vars the owner sets per environment under
  // "vars"; until they are set, minting a reply link or connecting a LINE
  // account answers 503 not_configured. LINE channel secrets and access
  // tokens never appear here: operators enter them per shop, and they go
  // straight into the encrypted credential vault. The LINE webhook stays
  // unreachable while officeInbound is off, like the Linear one.
  // The model gateway (docs/model-gateway.md): ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is a Wrangler
  // secret the owner adds (`wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`); until then
  // every model call answers 503 not_configured and nothing is sent. Two
  // optional vars, both the owner's decision: MODEL_SATANG_PER_USD (whole
  // satang per US dollar, 3500 when unset) and MODEL_DEFAULT_CAP_SATANG (each
  // shop's monthly cap in satang, 20000 when unset). None is set here yet.
  // Signing in by email (docs/pilot-api.md, "Signing in by email") is built
  // and off: both of its routes answer email_not_configured until the var
  // EMAIL_SIGN_IN is "on", a sender is bound and APPROVAL_LINK_SECRET is set.
  // The sender is Cloudflare Email Service's binding, "send_email" with the
  // name EMAIL, and the vars EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS and EMAIL_FROM_NAME, which
  // owners see. None of them is set in any environment: turning it on needs
  // the owner's yes, the Workers Paid plan and a sending domain the owner
  // controls. Its limiter, AUTH_CODE_LIMITER, is bound everywhere already, so
  // the route is limited before it answers even while it is off.
  // TEST_EMAIL_OUTBOX, like TEST_JWKS_JSON, belongs in wrangler.test.json
  // only: the dev deploy check refuses any config that sets a TEST_ var.
  // Google Sheets for Ton's books (docs/connectors.md, 4b): the owner's own
  // OAuth client, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, two Wrangler
  // secrets (`wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, then the secret). No
  // environment sets them yet, so every /v1/google route answers 503
  // google_not_configured and nothing reaches Google. The client's redirect
  // URI is PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN followed by /v1/google/callback.
  // Making a shop of one's own (docs/pilot-api.md, "Making a shop of your
  // own") is built and off: POST /v1/shops/new answers sign_ups_closed, and
  // reads nothing, until the var SELF_SERVE_SHOPS is "on". No environment sets
  // it: opening sign-ups is the owner's call. Its limiter,
  // SELF_SERVE_SHOP_LIMITER, is bound everywhere and counts only while it is on.
  // Artifact links (docs/pilot-api.md, "Artifact links") are built and off:
  // POST /v1/artifacts answers feature_disabled until the operator turns
  // artifactLinks on, and no page is served anywhere until the var
  // ARTIFACT_ORIGIN names a host of the links' own, never this one. No
  // environment sets ARTIFACT_LINKS or ARTIFACT_ORIGIN (docs/turning-on.md).
  // Skill links (item 84) are the same links for bundles of skills, behind
  // skillLinks as well (default the var SKILL_LINKS, which no environment
  // sets), so pages can be allowed and skills not.
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-16",
  // One origin for the pilot (docs/pilot-api.md): this Worker is the front
  // door. It answers /v1/* and /relay/* and hands every other path to the
  // pages Worker (wrangler.web.jsonc) over the WEB service binding, so the
  // console needs no CORS and one Cloudflare Access application covers the
  // console and the operator routes. This Worker must never get "assets":
  // Cloudflare runs a Worker with static assets behind an internal router that
  // does not pass ctx.access, and the admin gate needs it
  // (scripts/one-origin-contract.mjs refuses this file if "assets" appears).
  // Each environment names its own pages Worker; deploy that one first.
  "services": [{"binding": "WEB", "service": "manut-web"}],
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": false,
  // Metadata-only logs (task id, state, duration, status) — never bodies.
  // Sampling stays at 100% until the first production traffic is understood.
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  // Separate objects per environment from the first deploy: retrofitting
  // environments after production objects hold data is the expensive version.
  "env": {
    "dev": {
      "name": "manut-api-dev",
      "services": [{"binding": "WEB", "service": "manut-web-dev"}],
      // The owner's manut.xyz zone on Cloudflare (docs/decisions.md). The API
      // Worker owns the whole host as its custom domain and hands every page
      // to the pages Worker, so the links it mints point here too.
      "routes": [{"pattern": "dev.manut.xyz", "custom_domain": true}],
      "vars": {
        "WEB_ORIGIN": "https://dev.manut.xyz",
        "PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN": "https://dev.manut.xyz",
        // The audience of the Access application "Manut AI dev console"
        // (dev.manut.xyz/ops and dev.manut.xyz/v1/admin, allowing only the
        // owner's email). An audience tag identifies the application and is
        // not a secret.
        "ADMIN_ACCESS_AUD": "a7a8f9a7030979190c2a1dc2f2a5f518ae5530f9450dc8ad3f7dcaa1aa4a7cdf"
      },
      "durable_objects": {
        "bindings": [
          {"name": "TASK", "class_name": "TaskObject"},
          {"name": "AUTH", "class_name": "AuthObject"},
          {"name": "CRED", "class_name": "CredObject"},
          {"name": "SCHEDULES", "class_name": "ScheduleObject"},
          {"name": "TENANT", "class_name": "TenantObject"},
          {"name": "COMPANY", "class_name": "CompanyObject"},
          {"name": "RELAY", "class_name": "RelayObject"}
        ]
      },
      "ratelimits": [
        {
          "name": "AUTH_EXCHANGE_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112306",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 10,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // Asking for a sign-in code by email (email-code.ts), keyed and configured as the exchange's.
        {
          "name": "AUTH_CODE_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112334",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 10,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "AUTH_SESSION_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112307",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 60,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "LINEAR_INBOUND_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112308",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 300,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // Relay upgrade gates, keyed per IPv4 address or IPv6 /64 (A4b).
        // Proposed ids, unverified against the account like the rest.
        {
          "name": "RELAY_HOST_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112309",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 10,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "RELAY_PHONE_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112310",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 60,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // Manut AI pilot ingress (pilot.ts): LINE webhooks, keyed per source
        // address like the Linear webhook, and the owner's approval routes,
        // which the page polls while a send settles. Proposed ids, unverified
        // against the account like the rest.
        {
          "name": "LINE_INBOUND_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112323",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 300,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "PILOT_APPROVAL_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112324",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 120,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "OUTPOST_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112330",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 300,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GOOGLE_CALLBACK_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112338",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 30,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // Making a shop of one's own (self-serve.ts), per source address, counted only while sign-ups are open: the route
        // answers sign_ups_closed, and touches nothing, until SELF_SERVE_SHOPS is "on", which no environment sets.
        {
          "name": "SELF_SERVE_SHOP_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112342",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 10,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // A person's deletion of their own data (DELETE /v1/tenant/data), per source address, before the session is read.
        {
          "name": "TENANT_DELETE_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112346",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 10,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // Opening a shop session (POST /v1/shops/session, POST /v1/people/session), per signed-in person (session-limits.ts).
        {
          "name": "SHOP_SESSION_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112350",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 20,
            "period": 60
          }
        },
        // Artifact links' public read (artifacts.ts), every request on the artifact origin's host, per source address. The
        // host exists only once ARTIFACT_ORIGIN is set, which no environment does yet.
        {
          "name": "ARTIFACT_READ_LIMITER",
          "namespace_id": "2026112354",
          "simple": {
            "limit": 120,
            "period": 60
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "staging": {
      "name": "manut-api-staging",
      "services": [{"binding": "WEB", "service": "manut-web-staging"}],
      "durable_objects": {
        "bindings": [
          {"name": "TASK", "class_name": "TaskObject"},
